# META-DECISIONS

> Append-only log of every meta-agent PR + the user's verdict. The meta-agent reads this on each run to avoid re-proposing reverted changes.
>
> Generated by Night Shift Agent installer. Initial entry is empty.

## Schema

Each entry is a YAML block:

```yaml
- pr: <PR number>
  date_local: YYYY-MM-DD
  class: tactical | architectural | mixed
  auto_merged: true | false
  merged_at_utc: ISO timestamp
  pr_url: https://github.com/.../<N>
  files: [list of files touched]
  summary: <one-line>
  tactical_changes: [list]
  architectural_changes: [list]
  user_reverted: false      # flipped by future meta-runs reading git log
  user_modified: false
  do_not_touch: false       # User can set manually to refuse re-proposals
  notes: <auto + user-added>
```

## How the meta-agent uses this

- Before proposing any edit, meta-agent reads this file.
- For each entry with `user_reverted: true` OR `do_not_touch: true`:
  - Note the file(s) + intent.
  - DO NOT REINTRODUCE those changes.
- For each entry, meta-agent checks git log for non-`[meta-agent]` commits the user made:
  - If commit reverts lines a meta-PR added → flip `user_reverted: true`
  - If commit modifies lines a meta-PR added → flip `user_modified: true`

## How you (the user) intervene

- Merge an architectural draft → fine. The meta-agent's next run will log it here.
- Close + revert an architectural draft → meta-agent next run detects the revert via git log, flips `user_reverted: true`, won't re-propose.
- Set `do_not_touch: true` manually on an entry → that file region becomes off-limits permanently.

